    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures). The audit log confirms the new unified id, e.g. `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` + `27` (FY27) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `1` (Luhn CHK).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**New/changed identity logic**\n- **`MemberId.java`** (new helper): `format(region, fiscalYear, hash8)` concatenates `REGION + FY(2-digit) + HASH8` and appends a Luhn `CHK` over that string's digits. Also parses `region(...)` and `fiscalYearDigits(...)` back out of a member id (the fixed 11-char tail \u2014 FY+HASH8+CHK \u2014 lets REGION/FY be recovered; the collision `-<n>` suffix is the only `-`).\n- **`AssignOwnerMemberId.java`** (replaces `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` + `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber`): computes REGION (from postcode), FY (from registration date), HASH8 (SHA-256 over normalized-telephone + lastName \u2014 same hash as the region-and-hash identity), and applies **collision handling to the whole `memberId`** (`-2`, `-3`, \u2026).\n\n**Downstream references now use `memberId`**\n- **`OwnerMapper`**: dropped `checkDigit`; `locality` now derives REGION from `memberId` (so `ownerSegment` references it), and `fiscalYear` now derives FY from `memberId` \u2014 both falling back to postcode/city / registrationDate for seed data with no member id.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated`** + **`OwnerCreatedEvent`**: audit line and structured event now emit `memberId`.\n\n**Schema/spec**\n- `Owner` model: replaced the two columns with `member_id`.\n- All four `schema.sql` dialects: `member_id` replaces `customer_code` + `membership_number`.\n- `openapi.yml`: the three DTO fields replaced by a single documented `memberId`.\n- POST pipeline YAML: `assignCode`/`assignMembership` steps collapsed into one `assignMemberId` step.",
